  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "We define f(x)={f(x⊕reverse(x))+1if&nbsp;x≠00otherwisef(x)=\\begin{cases} f(x \\oplus  reverse(x))+1 &amp; \\text{if }  x \\neq 0 \\\\ 0 &amp; \\text{otherwise} \\end{cases}f(x)={f(x⊕reverse(x))+10​if&nbsp;x=0otherwise​\n\nHere, ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operation and reversereversereverse is a function that takes a postive integer, reverses its binary representation (without any leading zeros) and returns the resulting number. For example reverse(2)=1reverse(2)=1reverse(2)=1, reverse(6)=3reverse(6)=3reverse(6)=3, reverse(7)=7reverse(7)=7reverse(7)=7\n\nGiven an integer NNN, find out the value of ∑i=12N−1f(i)\\sum^{2^{N}-1}_{i=1}  f(i)∑i=12N−1​f(i) modulo 998244353998244353998244353 or claim that there exists a positive integer xxx &lt;2N\\lt 2^{N}&lt;2N for which fff is undefined.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT - the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case output a single line containing one integer :\n\n−1-1−1 if there exists a positive integer xxx such that x&lt;2Nx \\lt 2^Nx&lt;2N and f(x)f(x)f(x) is undefined\n∑i=12N−1f(i)\\sum^{2^{N}-1}_{i=1}  f(i)∑i=12N−1​f(i) modulo 998244353998244353998244353 otherwise",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤3⋅1051 \\leq T \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^51≤T≤3⋅105",
      "1≤N≤1091 \\leq N \\leq 10^91≤N≤109"
    ],
