        "explanation": "Explanation:\nNote that:\n\n\nf(1)=f(1⊕1)+1=f(0)+1=1f(1) = f(1 \\oplus 1) + 1 = f(0) + 1 = 1f(1)=f(1⊕1)+1=f(0)+1=1\n\n\nf(2)=f(2⊕1)+1=f(3)+1=(f(3⊕3)+1)+1=(f(0)+1)+1=2f(2) = f(2 \\oplus 1) + 1 = f(3) + 1 = (f(3 \\oplus 3) + 1) + 1 = (f(0) + 1) + 1 = 2f(2)=f(2⊕1)+1=f(3)+1=(f(3⊕3)+1)+1=(f(0)+1)+1=2\n\n\nf(3)=f(3⊕3)+1=f(0)+1=1f(3) = f(3 \\oplus 3) + 1 = f(0) + 1 = 1f(3)=f(3⊕3)+1=f(0)+1=1\n\n\nTest case-1: ∑i=121−1f(i)=f(1)=1\\sum^{2^{1}-1}_{i=1}  f(i) = f(1) = 1∑i=121−1​f(i)=f(1)=1. So answer is 1 mod 998244353=11 \\text{ mod } 998244353 = 11 mod 998244353=1.\n\n\nTest case-2: ∑i=122−1f(i)=f(1)+f(2)+f(3)=1+2+1=4\\sum^{2^{2}-1}_{i=1}  f(i) = f(1) + f(2) + f(3) = 1 + 2 + 1 = 4∑i=122−1​f(i)=f(1)+f(2)+f(3)=1+2+1=4. So answer is 4 mod 998244353=44 \\text{ mod } 998244353 = 44 mod 998244353=4."
